# Semantic and atomic commits

Every commit must use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) and contain a single logical change.

## Format

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body explaining why]
```

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.

- Imperative, lowercase description; no trailing period
- Optional scope in parentheses (`feat(proto):`, `ci:`, `chore(dart):`)
- Body is optional; use it for motivation, not a file list

```
# ❌ BAD
Add stuff and also fix CI
WIP
feat: Add the new Ledger type.

# ✅ GOOD
feat(proto): add processed ledger messages

ci: run buf lint via pre-commit
```

## Atomic

- One concern per commit: do not mix unrelated work (schema vs CI vs package metadata)
- Split independent changes; keep refactors separate from features
- If a change is hard to describe in one conventional subject, split it
